            <ArticleTitle>Transformation of Organostannanes Based on Photocleavage of C-Sn Bond via Single Electron Transfer Process.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>16559</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1038/s41598-017-16806-3</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In this work, we developed a new method for the transformation of organostannanes via radical process. In this reaction, highly reactive carbon radical species can be efficiently generated through HBr-catalyzed photocleavage of C-Sn bond via single electron transfer process. Under aerobic conditions, the in situ formed primary/secondary alkyl radicals can be further highly selectively oxidized into carboxylic acids/ketones, respectively.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
